@page "/"
<PageTitle>Tangent Atlas</PageTitle>

@* The home page is the first section only; the menu leads to a page for each of the others. *@
<section class="ta-hero">
    <div class="ta-container ta-hero-inner">
        <div class="ta-hero-head">
            <h1 class="ta-hero-title">A thermostat for <em>all</em> your money.</h1>
        </div>

        <div class="ta-hero-grid">
            <div class="ta-hero-copy">
                <div class="ta-hero-point">
                    <p class="ta-hero-lead">Connect your accounts and see everything you own and owe on one dashboard. Keep score the way professionals do, by risk as well as return. Set your rules, and every dollar coming in or going out follows them, so your money never runs too hot or too cold.</p>
                    <a href="/your-net-worth" class="ta-more-link">See Ken’s dashboard →</a>
                </div>
                <div class="ta-hero-point">
                    <p class="ta-hero-lead">Most portfolios aren’t plans. They’re accidents: a stock from a tip, a fund from an old job, cash wherever it landed. Turn yours into a plan: your own personal index. Choose how many companies you want to own and leave out the ones you’d rather not. Decide how much risk you want to take, then run it the way the big index funds run theirs: weighted by company size and rebalanced every quarter.</p>
                    <a href="/your-plan" class="ta-more-link">See what a plan would have done for Ken →</a>
                </div>
                <div class="ta-hero-point">
                    <p class="ta-hero-lead">A plan that only works when the sun is shining is half a plan. What happens when you lose your job, or get a margin call? You need cash, and you want to raise it as carefully as you built your portfolio. What do you sell first? What do you sell last? Make raising cash part of your plan.</p>
                    <a href="/when-the-storm-hits" class="ta-more-link">See how Ken raises cash →</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <RulesPanel />
        </div>

        <div class="ta-page-final ta-home-final">
            <p class="ta-page-close">Keep your bank and your broker. Lose the chaos.</p>
            <AuthorizeView>
                <NotAuthorized>
                    <a href="/signup" class="ta-btn ta-btn-primary ta-btn-large">Sign up</a>
                </NotAuthorized>
            </AuthorizeView>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
